1016 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (After reducing our six key features into three principal components, the customer points in PCA_ds form irregular, cloud-like groupings with long tails and outliers \(PC1 spans from 3.24 to 11.36\). K-Means forces spherical clusters that cut through these shapes, and DBSCAN either merges sparse segments or treats them as noise when tuning density parameters. Agglomerative Clustering, however, iteratively merges the closest points based purely on distance, so it naturally respects the true contours and varying densities of our data without imposing uniform cluster shapes.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
endobj
